## Chapter 0 — What This Volume Is, and Its Discipline

The brand was, until now, under-defined: a tagline, four colours, a font trio, and
one evocative idea (the waveform Z). That is enough to start but not enough to
build a coherent product or speak with one voice. This volume matures it into a
real system — verbal and visual — while holding the discipline the rest of the
Bible holds: **define what the Kampala MVP needs, mark the rest dormant.**

```
BRAND LAW (immutable — Stable Zone, founder-gated):
  The strategy below — positioning, essence, voice, the colour-as-information
  principle — is locked. It does not drift screen to screen.

BRAND SYSTEM (Adaptive within brand law — Architecture/Design Council):
  The visual specifics — exact type scale, token values, logo construction —
  may mature and be refined as the product is built, provided they never
  violate brand law.

DORMANT (do not build now):
  Sub-brand architecture (Zuka Ride, Zuka Pulse as products), multi-market
  brand adaptation, multi-language brand voice, campaign systems. Volume 24.
```

The test for any brand decision: *does this help build or market the actual
Kampala MVP?* If yes, it's here. If it's expansion-era, it's dormant.

