## Chapter 1 — Brand Strategy (LOCKED)

### Positioning Statement
```
For the people of a city who want to know where life is happening tonight —
and for the venues and organisers who make it happen —
ZUKA is the participation infrastructure that makes the city's live energy
visible, accessible, and worth remembering.
Unlike listings apps and ticketing tools that treat an event as a transaction,
ZUKA treats participation as something that compounds — into memories,
relationships, trust, and belonging.
```

### Brand Essence
```
THE CITY, ALIVE.
```
One idea beneath everything: ZUKA makes the living energy of a place visible and
joinable in real time. Not "find events." Not "buy tickets." *Feel the city come
alive, and step into it.*

### The Brand Promise
```
When something is happening, you'll know. When you arrive, you'll belong.
When it's over, it stays with you.
```

### Brand Personality (five traits, with their guardrails)
```
ALIVE         Energetic, present-tense, immediate.    Not manic or hype-y.
LOCAL         Of Kampala, in the language of Kampala.  Not parochial or excluding.
WARM          Welcoming, human, belonging-first.       Not saccharine or fake.
DIRECT        Plain, specific, honest.                 Not blunt or cold.
TRUSTWORTHY   Reliable, safe, transparent.             Not corporate or stiff.
```

### What ZUKA Is Not (positioning negatives — sharpen by contrast)
```
Not a social network   — participation is real-world; the app points outward.
Not a hype machine      — energy is shown by real signals, never manufactured.
Not a listings board     — a gathering is alive, not a static row.
Not Western-templated    — built for Kampala first, not adapted from the US/EU.
Not an attention trap     — it helps you go out, not stay scrolling.
```

