## Chapter 2 — Brand Origin & Name

```
ZUKA            from Sheng/Swahili "mzuka" — the electric vibe, the sudden
                surge of energy when a place comes alive.
Phonetics       ZOO-kah
Tagline         "The city just came alive."
Essence line    "The city, alive."  (shorter, for tight spaces)
```

The name is a feeling, not a function — deliberately. It carries the brand essence
in two syllables, in a register locals recognise. This is a strength: protect it.
Never back-explain the name in product copy ("ZUKA, your events app") — that
flattens a feeling into a category.

