## Chapter 3 — Verbal Identity (NEW — the biggest prior gap)

The voice was named but never operationalised. Here is the working system.

### Voice Principles (how ZUKA always sounds)
```
PRESENT-TENSE & IMMEDIATE   "47 events live in Kampala" — not "Discover events."
SPECIFIC OVER CLEVER        "8 spots in Kabalagala, 2km away" — not "Lots nearby!"
LOCAL-FIRST                 Real neighbourhoods, real venues, Kampala cadence.
WARM, NOT HYPED             "Sounds good?" — not "🔥 INSANE VIBES TONIGHT 🔥".
HONEST                      Never imply live-when-pre-launch or scale we lack.
SHORT                       Built for a phone. One idea per line.
```

### Messaging Hierarchy (what we lead with, in order)
```
1. WHAT'S ALIVE NOW     the live energy of the city (the hook, the differentiator)
2. EFFORTLESS ACCESS    discover with no wall; enter in 3 taps (the relief)
3. IT STAYS WITH YOU    memories, belonging, the compounding (the depth)
```
Lead with 1. Earn 2. Deepen to 3. Never open on depth-talk ("civilisational
participation infrastructure") to a person who just wants to know where to go.

### The "We Say / We Never Say" Table
```
WE SAY                              WE NEVER SAY
─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
"live now"                          "trending" / "viral"
"the city came alive"               "unlock amazing experiences"
"47 events live in Kampala"         "join thousands of users"
"Sounds good? 3 spots left."        "🔥 Don't miss out! Selling fast!! 🔥"
"Gathering" (semantic copy)         "event" used to mean something disposable
"a quiet night in Ntinda"           a blank empty state
"New Member" / "Trusted Organiser"  "Trust score: 84"
"free entry"                        "FREE!!!" with manufactured excitement
honest availability                 "live now" when it's pre-launch
```

### Naming Conventions (for features, so the product reads as one voice)
```
- Feature names are plain-English actions or living nouns:
  "Go Live" · "City Pulse" · "Heat Map" · "Live Wall" · "Vibe Drop" · "Crowd Meter"
- Avoid sub-branded jargon at MVP ("ZukaSense™"). Names describe, they don't trademark.
- A person is a Person; a community-scale event is a Gathering (UI may show
  "Events"); trust shows as a state, never a number. (Volume 03 Dictionary governs.)
```

### Microcopy Doctrine
```
Empty states give direction, never mood: name the nearest alive place + distance.
Errors are plain and recoverable: what happened, what to do, no blame.
CTAs are verbs the person wants: "Go Live", "Get Tickets", "Tune In".
Notifications obey the Notification Constitution (Vol 16): 6 categories,
quiet hours, max 2 discovery/day, grief-sensitive, no engagement-timing.
```

