## Chapter 4 — The Colour System (MATURING — built on the locked principle)

### Brand Law: Colour as Information (LOCKED)
ZUKA's single most distinctive visual decision. Colour is not decoration; it
*carries meaning*. This principle is immutable; the exact values may be refined
for accessibility.

```
INFORMATION COLOURS (semantic — meaning is fixed to the hue):
  Live Coral    #FF4D4D   LIVE RIGHT NOW. Reserved. Never decorative. Never
                          used for anything that is not currently live.
  Ember Gold    #F5A623   Starting soon · primary action · active/energy-rising.
  Kampala Forest #1A3A2A   Tonight · scheduled · calm-but-coming.
  Neutral        (greys)   Free entry · general info · the resting state.

BASE:
  Midnight      #0E0C0A   Primary background — "the city at 2am." The dark canvas
                          against which live energy glows.
```

### The System Around It (NEW — what was missing for real implementation)
A semantic principle needs a full palette to build against. Maturing additions
(Adaptive — Design Council may tune values, not meanings):

```
NEUTRAL RAMP (for text, surfaces, borders on the Midnight base):
  Ink-0  #0E0C0A  base background        Ink-3  #6B6863  secondary text
  Ink-1  #1A1815  raised surface/cards   Ink-4  #A8A49E  tertiary / disabled
  Ink-2  #2A2724  borders / dividers     Ink-5  #F2EFEA  primary text on dark

FUNCTIONAL STATES (distinct from information colours, to avoid overloading them):
  Success  #3A9D5C   confirmations (a ticket secured) — distinct from Forest
  Warning  #E08A2B   cautions — distinct from Ember Gold's "energy" meaning
  Error    #D64545   failures — distinct from Coral's "live" meaning
  Info     #4A90B8   neutral system messages

  NOTE: functional states are deliberately NOT the information colours. A failed
  payment must never wear Live Coral — Coral means LIVE, only and always.
```

### Accessibility (NEW — non-negotiable for the Africa-first baseline)
```
- All text/background pairs meet WCAG AA (4.5:1 body, 3:1 large) on Midnight.
- Information colour is NEVER the sole carrier of meaning — always paired with a
  label, icon, or position (colour-blind safety; ~8% of male users).
  "Live" = coral pill + the word "LIVE" + top position, not coral alone.
- Coral on Midnight and Gold on Midnight must be verified for contrast; darken
  text or add a surface behind small coloured text where needed.
```

