## Chapter 5 — Typography (MATURING)

### The Type Trio (LOCKED roles)
```
Space Grotesk   Display · wordmark · headlines · the City Pulse count.
                Carries personality and energy. Used big and confident.
Inter           Body · UI · labels · everything functional. Maximum legibility
                on a small, cheap screen. The workhorse.
Space Mono      Data · timestamps · counts · ticket codes. The "instrument
                readout" of a living system. Used sparingly, for precision.
```

### The Scale (NEW — was entirely absent; needed to build any screen)
A mobile-first modular scale, sized for a 2GB Android at arm's length:
```
ROLE          FONT           SIZE/LINE    WEIGHT     USE
Display       Space Grotesk  32 / 38      700        City Pulse hero, splash
H1            Space Grotesk  26 / 32      600        screen titles
H2            Space Grotesk  21 / 28      600        section heads
H3            Inter          18 / 24      600        card titles
Body          Inter          16 / 24      400        primary reading (min 16 — never smaller for body)
Body-strong   Inter          16 / 24      600        emphasis
Caption       Inter          14 / 20      400/500    metadata, helper text
Micro         Inter          12 / 16      500        legal, timestamps (use rarely)
Data          Space Mono     14 / 20      400        counts, codes, times
```
Rules: body text never below 16px (3G-era readability + accessibility). Line
length caps naturally on mobile. Space Grotesk never for long reading. Space Mono
never for prose.

### The Spacing Scale (RATIFIED 2026-07-18 — founder approval via the A-00 foundation sheet)
An 8px grid, logical px: `xs 4 · sm 8 · md 16 · lg 24 · xl 32 · xxl 48`.
Deliberately boring (standard Flutter/Material convention); canonical source
`lib/core/theme/zuka_spacing.dart`. Image weight budgets remain PROPOSED.

