## Chapter 6 — The Wordmark & Symbol (MATURING — spec, not just an idea)

### The Concept (LOCKED idea)
```
The Z rendered as a continuous waveform — simultaneously an oscilloscope trace,
a heartbeat, and the letter Z. When the city is alive, the Z pulses.
```

### Toward a Specification (NEW — Design Council to finalise construction)
The idea was never specified enough to draw consistently. The maturing brief:
```
FORM        A single unbroken stroke that reads as 'Z': the top bar, the
            diagonal as a waveform peak-and-trough, the bottom bar as the
            settled baseline. One continuous line — never disconnected segments.
PULSE       The diagonal's amplitude is the "alive" signal. At rest: a gentle
            wave. When live content is present (City Pulse active): the wave
            animates — a single travelling pulse, ~1.2s, never a frantic loop.
WEIGHT      Stroke weight derived from Space Grotesk's heavier weights so the
            mark sits in family with the wordmark.
CLEARSPACE  Minimum clear space = the height of the Z on all sides.
MIN SIZE    Legible at 24px (app icon corner, nav bar). Below that, use the
            simplified rest-state (no animation, simpler wave).
COLOUR      On Midnight: Ember Gold at rest; a single Coral pulse-frame may
            travel the wave when live content exists (the only decorative-
            adjacent use of Coral, and even here it signals "alive").
WORDMARK    "ZUKA" in Space Grotesk, tight-but-not-cramped tracking, the
            waveform-Z replacing or leading the literal Z. Lockup variants:
            horizontal (wordmark), symbol-only (app icon), stacked (splash).
```
This is a build brief, not a final lockup — generating the actual vector is a
Design Council task, gated by the Brand Law above.

